<title>BAHRAIN: Al Bank Al Saudi Al Fransi nine-month net falls.</title>
<headline>Al Bank Al Saudi Al Fransi nine-month net falls.</headline>
<dateline>MANAMA 1996-10-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Nine months to September 30, 1996</p>
<p>		    (billion Saudi riyals unless stated)</p>
<p> Net profit		  264.2 million   vs  279.2 million</p>
<p> Provisions		   60.0 million   vs   30.0 million</p>
<p> Net operating income    248.8 million   vs  274.0 million</p>
<p> Operating income	    1.45	    vs    1.51</p>
<p> Operating expenses	  1.20	    vs    1.24</p>
<p> Shareholders' equity	2.65	    vs    2.54</p>
<p> Net loans and advances    8.79	    vs    9.58</p>
<p> Customer deposits	  17.07	    vs   16.39</p>
<p> Assets			 27.71	    vs   26.93</p>
<p>Full Name: Al Bank Al Saudi Al Fransi, also known as Saudi French Bank.</p>
<p>Note - Banque Indosuez, the banking arm of Compagnie de Suez owns 31.1 percent of the Riyadh-based bank, which has doubled its paid-in capital this year to 1.8 billion riyals by issuing bonus shares on a one-for-one basis, paid for from reserves.</p>
</text>
